First, you need to install the `cors` package in your Wordpress project. If you're using a managed WordPress hosting service, you might not be able to modify the server directly. In that case, consider creating a custom endpoint using a plugin like "WP REST API CORS" or "Advanced CORS Manager." These plugins can help you manage CORS headers without modifying the server configuration.

