\section*{Description of the Issue}
We are experiencing technical difficulties with the integration of the XYZ API into our multi-tiered system architecture. Specifically, we encounter an error message "API Key Invalid" (Error Code: 403) when attempting to authenticate requests. This issue occurs intermittently and affects multiple applications within our system.

\section*{System Architecture}
\begin{table}[h!]
\centering
\caption{System Architecture Overview}
\label{tab:systemArchitecture}
\begin{tabular}{|l|l|}
\hline
Layer & Description \\ \hline
Presentation & User Interface \\ \hline
Application & Business Logic \\ \hline
Integration & API Integration \\ \hline
Database & Data Storage \\ \hline
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

The API integration layer is responsible for handling communication between our internal systems and the XYZ API. We have implemented this integration using the HTTPS protocol and cURL library in PHP. Our current implementation includes the following steps:

1. Obtain an API key from the XYZ API website.
2. Store the API key securely in a database.
3. Retrieve the API key from the database during API requests.
4. Set the API key as a header in the cURL request.
5. Send the API request using cURL.
6. Parse the API response and process data as needed.

\section*{Analysis of Potential Root Causes}
Upon investigation, we suspect that one or more of the following factors may contribute to the issue:

\begin{itemize}
