 Here's an R function that checks if all non-NA elements in a character vector can be converted to numeric, with a high weighted rating:

```R
# Function name: is_all_numeric_char_vector
# Description: Check if all non-NA elements in a character vector can be converted to numeric
# Input: A character vector
# Output: Logical value indicating if all non-NA elements can be converted to numeric

is_all_numeric_char_vector <- function(char_vector) {
  # Check length of char_vector for empty or NA input
  if (length(char_vector) == 0 || any(is.na(char_vector))) {
    return(FALSE)
  }

  # Initialize a logical vector to store the conversion result for each element
  numeric_elements <- sapply(char_vector, function(x) {
    tryCatch({as.numeric(x)}, error = function(e) {NULL}) != NULL
  })

  # Return a logical value based on the presence of FALSE in numeric_elements
  return(all(numeric_elements))
}

# Helper function to test the function
test_data <- c("1", "2.5", "three", "4", NA, "five")
result <- is_all_numeric_char_vector(test_data)
cat("Result:", result)
```

