 To create a simple toast notification using React and the useContextHook, follow these steps:

First, let's create a custom ToastContext provider and its component:

1. Create a new file `ToastContext.js`:

```javascript
import { createContext, useState } from "react";

export const ToastContext = createContext();

export const ToastProvider = ({ children }) => {
  const [message, setMessage] = useState("");
  const [isVisible, setIsVisible] = useState(false);

  const showToast = (message) => {
    setMessage(message);
    setIsVisible(true);

    // Hide toast after some time (you can adjust the timeout as needed)
    setTimeout(() => {
      setMessage("");
      setIsVisible(false);
    }, 3000);
  };

  return (
    <ToastContext.Provider value={{ showToast }}>
      {children}
      {isVisible && <div className="toast">{message}</div>}
    </ToastContext.Provider>
  );
};
```

This code sets up a state for the message and visibility of the toast, as well as a function called `showToast` that updates these states. It also renders the toast when it is visible.

