  height: 300px; /* replace this value with your preferred height */
}
```

5. Save the `custom.scss.liquid` file, then clear your theme cache by clicking on Online Store > Themes > Actions > Clear Cache.

6. Finally, compile the Sass files by navigating to Online Store > Themes > Actions > Compile Assets.

After completing these steps, the images in the "feature-row__image" elements with the given class names should now be smaller in size according to the specified dimensions in your custom CSS.

